nv-define-space2-dispatch: TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2 unmarshals publicInfo into publicInfo

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, Table "TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2 Command"):
"TPM2B_AUTH | auth | the authorization value", "TPM2B_NV_PUBLIC_2 |
publicInfo | the public parameters of the NV area".

The command's dispatch table (CommandDispatch.inl) unmarshals the second
parameter, the TPM2B_NV_PUBLIC_2, at the offset of the auth member instead of
publicInfo: publicInfo stays zero (handleType 0, so every well-formed command
fails with TPM_RC_HANDLE + publicInfo) and the authValue is overwritten. The
entry now targets publicInfo, so TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2 defines an ordinary NV
Index like TPM2_NV_DefineSpace (as the public tcgtpm, ibmswtpm2 and tpm-rs do).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
@@ -2546,7 +2546,9 @@
     MAKE_DISPATCH_SEPARATOR(START_INPUT_PARAMETERS),
     // Command input parameters
     MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_AUTH, auth),
-    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_NV_PUBLIC_2, auth),
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // publicInfo was unmarshaled into the auth member.
+    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_NV_PUBLIC_2, publicInfo),
 
     MAKE_DISPATCH_SEPARATOR(START_OUTPUT_HANDLES),
     // Response output handles
